  "summary": {
    "intent": "Fix apps/validate's RDT oracle (crashing on typescript@7 import) with a separate TypeScript 6 API, then build a semantic probe via typescript@next's tsc-api and re-verify the type-checker-integration doc's Evidence numbers against the full fixture corpus (stopping before Rust client work). Later, investigate and clean up a large pile of unrelated uncommitted repo changes (AGENTS.md migration, semantic-model relocation, doc prose) discovered via the `entire` search tool.",
    "outcome": "RDT now resolves against typescript@6.0.3 via a `typescript-next: npm:typescript@next` aliased dependency (pnpm-workspace overrides didn't actually take effect); wrote run-semantic.ts and parity.ts, re-ran the full 44-file/47-component corpus (99.7% required-prop match, 95.3% type-string match), and updated docs/type-checker-integration.md. Traced the unrelated uncommitted pile to a prior session via `entire checkpoint explain`, ran 4 parallel cleanup agents (ADR, root docs, topic docs, semantic-model relocation), fixed remaining flagged issues, and committed everything as two logical commits (a8875cb docs/AGENTS.md migration + prose cleanup, and a second commit moving .claude/semantic-model to docs/architecture).",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "apps/validate uses console.log/console.error as its style convention (not chalk, despite it being a dependency) — the crates/cli AGENTS.md 'no println!, use output.rs' rule is Rust-CLI-specific and doesn't apply to this Node/TS harness",
        "pnpm-workspace.yaml `overrides` entries get recorded in pnpm-lock.yaml but don't actually rewrite peer dependency resolution in this pnpm version (11.9.0) — use an aliased dependency (`name: npm:pkg@tag`) instead to force a specific version for one consumer",
        "typescript@next ships a `typescript/unstable/async` module (API/Checker/Program classes, async methods) that is a full JS wrapper, not raw JSON-RPC; SyntaxKind/TypeFlags/SymbolFlags live in `typescript/unstable/ast` and `typescript/dist/enums/*.enum.js`, not the async module",
        "react-docgen-typescript 2.4.0 has a real bug: multiple forwardRef components in one file (fixtures/rdt-compat/svg-icon.tsx) cross-contaminate element types between components",
        "docs/adr/README.md defines house style for the whole repo (banned words list: leverage/utilize/robust/essentially/seamless; sentence-case headers; active voice; no filler) — cleanup agents applied this repo-wide, not just to ADRs",
        "this repo's convention: .claude/, .codex/, .gemini/, .agents/, .github/hooks|skills/ are per-tool config dirs; shared docs must live in AGENTS.md/docs/ so every agent tool can read them, not just Claude Code — callisto (sibling repo) already made this same .claude/semantic-model → docs/architecture/ move for the same reason",
        "docs/archive/ is the repo's convention for retiring stale planning docs, with a README index; archived docs should not have internal paths rewritten to match current state (treated like not rewriting ADR history)",
        "`entire checkpoint explain --session <id>` and `entire search --json --compact` can reconstruct provenance of uncommitted changes across prior sessions when git history alone doesn't explain them"
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "apps/validate/src/run-semantic.ts",
          "finding": "Reimplements RDT's extraction algorithm using typescript@next's async Checker API; refactored from an await-in-loop pattern to Promise.all-based parallelism to satisfy oxlint's no-await-in-loop/no-nested-ternary rules, verified output-identical (ignoring Symbol.iterator id noise) after refactor"
        },
        {
          "path": "apps/validate/src/parity.ts",
          "finding": "New script diffing run-semantic.ts output against the committed RDT baseline; wired into `pnpm parity`"
        },
        {
          "path": "apps/validate/package.json",
          "finding": "typescript stays ^6.0.3 for RDT's peer dep; added typescript-next as npm:typescript@next alias for the semantic probe's own use"
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "When multiple background subagents report via teammate-message notifications, dedupe idle_notification pings that just restate an already-reported summary rather than re-summarizing to the user",
        "For causally-chained work (broken tool blocked the probe, which blocked the re-run), commit as one unit rather than splitting by step, but split truly unrelated concurrent work (doc/AGENTS.md migration) into its own separate commit(s)",
        "When investigating stale/uncommitted changes with unclear origin, `entire search` + `entire checkpoint explain --session <id>` can trace them back to the originating conversation and its actual prompts far faster than guessing from diff content alone"
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "pnpm-workspace.yaml overrides silently failed to rewrite peer resolution despite being written to the lockfile, requiring several install/verify cycles (including a full node_modules + lockfile wipe) before switching to the aliased-dependency approach",
      "Had to reverse-engineer typescript@next's undocumented `typescript/unstable/async` API by reading minified/compiled dist JS directly (api.js, node.js) since no docs exist for the TS7 tsc-api yet",
      "SyntaxKind import initially failed because it's not re-exported from typescript/unstable/async, only from typescript/unstable/ast — cost a debug cycle",
      "Large unrelated pile of uncommitted changes (AGENTS.md migration, semantic-model, ADRs) sitting in the working tree caused confusion about scope and required a full investigation via `entire` before it could be safely separated from the oracle-fix commit"
    ],
    "open_items": [
